Z||000006||Bill Osmer||11-25-1999||01:30 PM||||SloPonti -<P>I've been experimenting with colored lines, too. I've seen some very nice custom Fieros (at the NIFE Fierorama last fall) that had color-coordinated schemes (pearl white paint, with turquoise trim - changed the black exterior molding as well as the corregated wire looms in the front and rear - looked great).<P>I have, unfortunately, little imagination for this, but I appreciate good ones when I see them. I'm dreaming about changing mine. I have a silver GT fastback. I think a metalic blue would be a good trim color. <P>Now for my experiment: since there's limited colors available, I've tried painting the pieces I want. First - clean real good, then prime with quality primer, then finally at least two coats of desired color.<P>What do you think? Have you tried this approach?||||reg||1
